The camera has moved in close to the far bank and stands level with two men who are walking out of the tall grass toward it, on the same patch of bank where the three men stand in @place.

@explorer on the LEFT: the TALLER of the two, a bearded European of 1537 in a soft maroon-red cloth cap with no brim, long dark wavy hair, a grey-mauve quilted doublet belted at the waist, maroon knee breeches, pale hose, tall brown boots, a blade sheathed on his belt, hands empty.
@guide on the RIGHT: the SHORTER of the two, clearly shorter than the explorer, a lean young indigenous man, bare chest, dark bob-cut hair with a fringe, a cream cloth wrap at the waist, barefoot, hands empty.

Both are full figure, head to feet in frame, each about HALF the frame height, mid-stride, walking toward the camera, looking ahead past it. Behind them the same tall grass and the same wall of rainforest as @place, seen from much closer. The bottom edge of the frame is the grassy lip of the bank: NO WATER is visible, not a strip. There is no third man in this frame.

Plain hard tropical daylight exactly as in @place — no haze, no mist, no god rays, no sun shafts, no glow, no bloom. Photographic: real skin, real cloth, real leaves, natural depth of field, fine film grain. Not a painting, not an illustration, not a render. No text, no border, no letterbox bars.

